                    {
                        "form_id": "2dc13110-2094-437c-aa5a-a5cc5eb50586",
                        "entry_id": "fbffc64e-c64f-3518-aa9f-50323cda4ef4",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "магнитосфе́рах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c316a7a-e10c-3db6-a2d6-7ce1e138947c",
                        "entry_id": "fbffc64e-c64f-3518-aa9f-50323cda4ef4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "астрон. магнитная оболочка небесного тела; область пространства вокруг небесного тела, в которой поведение окружающей тело плазмы определяется магнитным полем этого тела"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2852881f-add0-4ced-8784-3082df2c88b9",
                                "sense_id": "3c316a7a-e10c-3db6-a2d6-7ce1e138947c",
                                "text": "Методами наземной радиоастрономии впервые удалось обнаружить мощную магнитосферу на Юпитере."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54c61b30-6d1c-42d9-9f53-c644b7d70cd5",
                                "sense_id": "3c316a7a-e10c-3db6-a2d6-7ce1e138947c",
                                "text": "Мощные процессы изменения конфигурации магнитного поля и движения плазмы в магнитосфере являются причиной магнитных бурь, полярных сияний, нарушений радиосвязи, появления индукционных токов в линиях электропередачи, в телефонных и телеграфных сетях."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f587e5d9-cfbd-402e-8238-32c8ea012044",
                        "source_entry_id": "fbffc64e-c64f-3518-aa9f-50323cda4ef4",
                        "source_sense_id": "3c316a7a-e10c-3db6-a2d6-7ce1e138947c",
                        "target_lang_word": "magnetosphere",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "magnetosphere",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "679cb3de-3378-37bd-82ea-8aa9c55b3a7d",
                                        "entry_id": "a1e624a1-735f-3a36-a035-00f9df86a30e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The comet-shaped region around Earth or another planet in which charged particles are trapped or deflected. Shaped by the solar wind and the planet's magnetic field."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f448ed9b-094c-4ab6-b158-a6b7475942fc",
                                                "sense_id": "679cb3de-3378-37bd-82ea-8aa9c55b3a7d",
                                                "text": "We derive rotation periods, photometric activity indices, flaring energies, mass loss rates, gyrochronological ages, X-ray luminosities and consider implications for the planetary magnetospheres and habitability."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e705c22-61c6-45e9-ba38-43e0564db878",
                                                "sense_id": "679cb3de-3378-37bd-82ea-8aa9c55b3a7d",
                                                "text": "One of the earliest (and biggest) space weather events on record occurred in September 1859, when a massive solar eruption crashed into the Earth's magnetosphere, triggering a geomagnetic storm that lasted for days."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c26e94c-a534-460e-8c53-9e07f4fa1ce8",
                                                "sense_id": "679cb3de-3378-37bd-82ea-8aa9c55b3a7d",
                                                "text": "Earth is surrounded by a magnetosphere — an invisible bubble of magnetism generated by the powerful churning of molten metals at Earth’s core. It prevents our atmosphere from being stripped away by solar winds blasting it from the sun. While the magnetosphere has been a constant presence for billions of years, its strength waxes and wanes over time."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
